# R5-2: a binding at the root -- `[]: b a` holds the root's own Array a; a write through b is seen through a and
# `length(b)` is a's.  The root is built in both modes (natively and with the root walked).  Entry 7.
[]: int a 3
[]: b a
b[1]: 6
if: length(b) != 3U || a[1] != 6
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 81; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
